{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Rotation evidence (no secret values recorded):\n\n- `/rebar/prod/github-replication-deploy-key`: SSM SecureString version 3 -> 4. New GitHub deploy key registered on `navapbc/rebar` as `rebar-gerrit-replication-20260907`, id `162586778`, write-enabled, fingerprint `SHA256:iJ7j98LfAGhV+gz4JpEOuCSDAAZUYR9FPuayfCSwW9c`. On-box deploy key materialized. Replication verified by Gerrit change 2806 reaching GitHub mirror (`origin/main` and Gerrit `main` both `665d1d0480187380f82e59bd95af1f0c44274732`). Retired old GitHub deploy key id `155914477` deleted after that verification.\n- `/rebar/prod/ci-gerrit-ssh-key`: SSM version 2 -> 3. New public key added to Gerrit account `rebar-ci-bot`, fingerprint `SHA256:EKxOTD5485sC94LFGGmP4XozhnpiQD8LjsTIliqEHww`. GitHub Actions secret `GERRIT_SSH_PRIVKEY` updated. SSH proof with new key returned Gerrit `3.14.1`. Old Gerrit SSH key comment `rebar-ci-gerrit` removed.\n- `/auth-solutions/COOKIE_SIGNING_SECRET`: SSM version 2 -> 3 using the documented 48-character openssl/base64 filtering convention. Auth-host Terraform `apply -replace=aws_lambda_function.auth_host` completed (Lambda recreated; API integration updated). The replace dropped the API Gateway invoke permission, causing `/authorize` 500 during smoke; I restored `AllowApiGatewayInvoke` for API `q8mv4bhkmh`. Final smoke: CloudFront `/authorize` returns 302 to Google (location redacted); direct execute-api probe returns 403 as expected. Active SSO sessions are invalidated as expected.\n- `/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key`: SSM version 3 -> 4. New Rebar Bot identity key was added with signed KEY_ADD under identity `594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d`; old key remains registered for historical signatures. New fingerprint `SHA256:oGCqzgfDMpDXRIhYIcmWrYulDr0dVEZLAoJhk2PRxkE`. GitHub Actions secret `REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY` updated. On-box `fetch-secrets.sh` materialized the new private key; review-bot container recreated and health OK.\n- `/rebar/prod/opcert-ed25519-key`: SSM version 3 -> 4. New public key fingerprint `SHA256:biqEFL9T969c1ADwEKw1KabRGvF4K6qMyxx1ZlpE77o` added to `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` for env `9f1c8e42-7a3b-4d5e-b6c1-2f0a9d8e7c65` via Gerrit change 2806; change passed LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 and was submitted. After GitHub mirror replication, private key was written to SSM, secrets were rematerialized, opcert was recreated, and MCP was blue/green flipped to live port 8092. MCP `/health` reports `opcert.matched=true`.\n\nRedeploy / health:\n- Secrets-only rematerialization ran on instance `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`: `materialize-deploy-key.sh`, `fetch-secrets.sh`, review-bot recreate, opcert recreate, and MCP blue/green cutover. `rebar-autodeploy.timer` was disabled only during manual recreate windows and is enabled/active again; service idle.\n- Internal health: Gerrit container remained up (not restarted), review-bot `/health` status OK/in_flight 0/queue_depth 0, opcert `/health` OK, MCP live `/health` store present, handshake OK, opcert matched true.\n- External health: Gerrit root HTTP 200, review-bot `/review/health` HTTP 200, MCP `/mcp` HTTP 401 unauthenticated (expected healthy auth boundary), SSO `/authorize` HTTP 302 to Google (redacted).\n\nCarve-outs / deferred items recorded from operator instruction: GitHub OAuth client id/secret and `/auth-solutions/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` were not rotatable by this operator context; `gerrit-ssh-host-ed25519-key` remains deferred because rotating it breaks clients' known_hosts.\n\nGerrit P1 coordination: no Gerrit restart and no Gerrit git-data mutation were performed; only review flow/replication and non-Gerrit service redeploys were touched.\n"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788824441505544001,"uuid":"d2227029-4f86-4334-a6f0-402f59200cc8"}